      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Taking both at once is **not recommended** because DayQuil already contains acetaminophen (the same active ingredient as Tylenol), so you risk accidentally doubling up and exceeding safe limits, especially with a 1000mg dose. Even though 4000mg is the daily max, taking a large single dose can strain your liver, and combining products makes it easy to lose track. Check the DayQuil label for its acetaminophen content, and if you need relief, space out doses or stick to one product at a time. For a bad flu, also consider drinking plenty of fluids and resting—if symptoms worsen, see a doctor.",
